# Public-API reference example — ships in docs, not in the package
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenDataProviderExample.cls
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenDataProviderExample.cls-meta.xml

# Einstein-only. These reference ConnectApi.EinsteinLLM, which is NOT a visible
# type in an org without the Einstein entitlement — deploying them there fails
# with "Type is not visible: ConnectApi.EinsteinLLM", and because deploys are
# atomic that takes the ENTIRE deploy down with it (measured 2026-07-26 against
# Portwood Dev: 409/411, full rollback). Fenced off so no package build can pick
# them up and break a subscriber who does not have Einstein.
#
# The rest of the feature is unaffected: DocGenAiProviderFactory resolves this
# class by name via Type.forName and falls back to DocGenUnavailableProvider, so
# the Designer simply hides the button. Deploy these two explicitly, by path, to
# an Einstein-enabled org:
#   sf project deploy start -o <einstein-org> \
#     -d force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProvider.cls \
#     -d force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProviderTest.cls
# Before this can ship in the base package, confirm whether a managed-package
# INSTALL behaves like a source deploy here — that is still unmeasured.
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProvider.cls
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProvider.cls-meta.xml
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProviderTest.cls
force-app/main/default/classes/DocGenEinsteinProviderTest.cls-meta.xml